    "# AHR · 30-case Luna experiment with environmental noise and patient/staff context · agentic vs non-agentic\n",
    "\n",
    "> **16 October 2026 · run-continuation amendment (not a new study condition).** The initial full-stage snapshot contained `FORMAL_006/agent/r1 = INPUT_SIZE_STOP`. A conservative local size estimator blocked the *unsent* correction request and the original notebook erroneously treated that per-workflow condition as a global halt. This copy excludes only `INPUT_SIZE_STOP` from the global halt set. It leaves the recorded invalid execution intact, skips every previously saved result, and executes only `NOT_RUN` combinations. All other global halt guards, model calls, evidence, cases, prompts, tools, validation rules, pricing limits, run identity and `RUN_LABEL` are unchanged. The recovery is documented as an execution-control deviation in the study audit; do not erase the original ZIP or override the failed response.\n",
    "\n",
    "**To continue:** reopen this notebook in Colab with the existing Google Drive mounted, set `RUN_STAGE='full'`, `APPROVE_PAID_CALLS=True` and `USE_GOOGLE_DRIVE=True`, and choose **Runtime → Run all**. Keep `RUN_LABEL = 'AHR_Luna30_ContextNoise_20261015_v4'` unchanged. The archived `INPUT_SIZE_STOP` remains invalid; this is *not* a retrial. No paid calls occur with the default OFF controls.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Master's project · 15 October 2026 · new context/noise dataset revision · paid calls OFF by default.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the **same `openai/gpt-6-luna` model through OpenRouter/OpenAI**, with our existing evidence table, output schema, tools and validator, in two conditions on **30 WESAD-recorded physiological scenarios**. There are **five repeats per condition per case**: **30 × 2 × 5 = 300 workflow executions**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important research assumptions.** These are *30 software evaluation scenarios*, not 30 independent patients: they use 15 WESAD participant recordings in adjacent 5-minute reference and current windows. Hospital context (including qualitative ambient noise and patient/staff context notes) is hypothetical. For **27 cases**, HR, RMSSD and EDA are explicitly assumed usable as hypothetical software inputs. **Three cases deliberately test partial data:** `FORMAL_006` has missing current EDA; `FORMAL_016` has missing reference RMSSD; `FORMAL_022` supplies current HR with `POOR` quality (value retained but comparison unavailable). These are **synthetic input-quality scenarios**, not independent validation of the original WESAD recordings. Two original numeric WESAD values are masked as `null` only in model/nurse inputs; source measurements remain unchanged in researcher-only provenance. No imputation is used. Two source pairs have documented development recording overlap; particularly S7, so include a **28-case non-overlap sensitivity subset** in analysis. No inference about physiological health/clinical effectiveness, and no claim that one nurse is clinical ground truth. The current source file is a provisional researcher release, not externally validated. Test-purpose labels remain researcher-only and are not supplied to either model workflow or the nurse. Do not change the inputs on the basis of formal model responses.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run sequence** (edit just two controls in Cell 2):\n",
    "\n",
    "1. `RUN_STAGE='offline'`, `APPROVE_PAID_CALLS=False`: click **Run all**, check all offline tests pass. No key or paid calls needed. Set `USE_GOOGLE_DRIVE=True` if you want results to survive a Colab runtime reset.\n",
    "2. Edit `RUN_STAGE='smoke'`, `APPROVE_PAID_CALLS=True`, **Run all** again. This performs **two paid workflows on the previous development case `PILOT_201`**, not on a formal case. It tests API/provider functionality and validation. This is *not* part of the 300.\n",
    "3. Once smoke shows **both VALID_SIMULATION**, edit `RUN_STAGE='full'` and **Run all** again. Completes/resumes the 300 workflows. It will never repeat an already saved result with the same run identity. A failure of one LLM answer remains a recorded result; a provider/budget stop halts further requests.\n",
    "4. Download **`AHR_LUNA30_CONTEXT_V4_RESULTS.zip`** at the end (the notebook attempts download; it also saves to Drive if enabled), and upload it to ChatGPT to analyse. The ZIP contains no API keys. **Full nurse-alignment scoring comes after we receive the nurse's independent responses**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Controls:** $5 USD local cumulative spending ceiling, $0.08 local per-request reservation maximum, 120-second timeout *per request*, provider pinned to `OpenAI`, maximum 6 agent calls and 8 tools, at most one revision, 16,384 output-token cap. These are *local safeguards*, not an account-wide billing guarantee. Earlier Luna pilot cost about USD $0.02 for ten workflows; today's total may differ.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**Master case dataset:** 27 fully observed cases plus three deliberate missing/unreliable scenarios. The unmasked original values are unchanged, the two masked original source values are researcher-only, and all baseline/current windows are adjacent. The exact embedded input JSON SHA-256 is `a09d532e3d6d8bcd051e91699d3fb9f933a1f0ae565f6d0f159fc2cb7c735b8b`. This case master must not be edited after the formal run starts.\n"
